 do anything queen captures on d6  we simply play bishop to g6 check and we  continue with our attack queen h7 oh  sorry not queen h7 check bishop captures  here king to f8 and now we capture this  pawn as well  and now the black king is completely  open there are no defenses here and  we're going to very quickly win this  game  another thing after rook to d6 of course  you don't have to capture you could play  some like rook 8 to d8 but now we just  capture on e6 this is also perfectly  fine and black is getting destroyed here  if you capture the rook of course the  bishop g6 check king g8 queen h7 czech  king f8 and now queen to h8 to check  king e7 and of course queen captures and  g7 will be checked made the pawn covers  the d6 square so like we said bishop  captures an h7 this doesn't work this  doesn't work so we might as well capture  it but now we play bishop to f6 and now  it's a completely different story now  queen captures on g7 will be checkmate  if you defend with rook to g8 queen to  h5 will be checkmate because the king  will not be able to retreat to the g8  square so your only option is to capture  the bishop and after the bishop is  captured we're going to play e captures  on f6 now again threaten mate here uh  it's  the exact same thing if rook blocks then  this will be checkmate so you have to  capture on f6 and now simply rook to d3  and this is how we deliver checkmate  there's nothing black can do about this  he can play some silly moves uh like  just you know some like queen e5 to try  and interpose but it will only prolong  mate for a few moves  uh so  uh that's uh the position hope you guys  enjoyed that and the previous one i i  really enjoyed both of them and if you  guys uh  enjoy videos like these uh do mention in  the comments if you enjoy more of them  because like i said these uh positions  are much much different than the ones  that would occur uh in modern games and  maybe you can learn a little bit more on  how to think how to ap